														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4813379">
									

<p>Disclaimer: I am not an experienced reviewer, nor am I that familiar with Dr. Gears. This is just my opinion as an average audience member.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Concept</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Concept</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Most basically, I think the beginning and end were done well but the middle could use some work. While I liked that you showed the personal impact of a containment breach, the cause of the breach confuses me. I didn’t really like the fact that Gears was just throwing Scranton Reality Anchors at the problem, also is this implying that Reality Anchors are a way to contain 106 and the foundation just isn’t using them? Maybe instead of being a containment procedure this whole thing could be a way to get 106’s slime. So it was always meant to be temporary but it just stopped working sooner than expected or the d-class messed it up.</p>
<p>I was also bothered by the bit with his dad. First, maybe I’m missing something but I thought his dad was dead. Now you’re saying that he’s an O5 member? Also, I think we need a better explanation as to how Gears found out the identity of one of the O5s. I was under the impression that was a really well kept secret.</p>
<p>I do think there should be more explanation between 5 and 6. Are Mary and Gears married? Was this baby planned? How long after the previous section was this? Maybe if you have him start to remember what’s happening it would clue us in too.</p>
<p>Overall though, I think the plot’s good. I like the way you shift Gears’ character, it somehow feels both sudden and natural at the same time. The way you portray him losing his friends after the breach is great too. I even wish I had a bit more of that.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Execution</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Execution</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I’m noticing a lot of very minor grammar mistakes. It’s means “it is”, its is the possessive. You sometimes shift from second person to third person, like the sentence “It made you feel genuine, as though he really was a top-level researcher”.</p>
<p>The cross-link from that section also confused me. When you reference 408 it made me start thinking the main character was Kondraki. After all, Gears is never mentioned in that article.</p>
<p>A few more minor fixes: “Brakes too slow” not “Brakes to slow” and “Dissected butterflies and put them into small little trays and forget about them.” should be forgot.</p>
<p>I loved the circular description you did with the car where you referenced how it changed from 1 to 5. Overall, I think your greatest strength was your descriptive nature. Not only did it give us a vivid image but it also showed us what Gears was paying attention to.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

